---
/**
 * Homepage Quick Example: intro + CSV side-by-side on tablet/desktop.
 */
import { Aside } from '@astrojs/starlight/components';
import DocImage from './DocImage.astro';
import CopyableCsv from './CopyableCsv.astro';
import bar2D from '../assets/bar-2D.png';
---

<div class="quick-example">
	<div class="quick-example__lead">
		<div class="quick-example__copy">
			<p>
				Point Vizb at a CSV. Numeric columns become charts. Categorical columns become
				axes when you group (or when auto-group picks one for you).
			</p>
			<p>
				After <a href="/getting-started/install">install</a>, chart a table like this:
			</p>
		</div>
		<div class="quick-example__csv">
			<CopyableCsv
				filename="sales.csv"
				csv={`region,product,quantity
West,Widget,39
West,Gear,20
South,Widget,15
South,Sensor,47
North,Gear,43
North,Widget,28
East,Sensor,31
East,Gear,22
Central,Widget,35
Central,Sensor,19`}
			/>
		</div>
	</div>

	<pre class="quick-example__code"><code>vizb bar sales.csv -g region,product -p x,y -o sales.html</code></pre>

	<p>
		Open <code>sales.html</code> in a browser. You get a grouped bar chart: region on X, product
		as series, height = <code>quantity</code>.
	</p>

	<DocImage src={bar2D} alt="2D grouped bar chart with product series per region" />

	<p>Flags in this example:</p>
	<ul>
		<li><code>bar</code> — one chart type (smallest learning path)</li>
		<li><code>sales.csv</code> — the table above (use <strong>Copy CSV</strong> to grab it)</li>
		<li><code>-g region,product</code> — columns that become dimensions</li>
		<li><code>-p x,y</code> — first group column → X, second → Y series</li>
		<li><code>-o sales.html</code> — self-contained HTML</li>
	</ul>

	<p>
		No <code>-g</code>? Vizb auto-groups a high-cardinality categorical column and logs the
		choice. Override whenever the guess is wrong.
	</p>

	<pre class="quick-example__code"><code>vizb bar sales.csv -o sales.html</code></pre>

	<p>
		From a clone of the Vizb repo, the full sample is <code>examples/csv/sales.csv</code> (~500
		orders across 2024–2025).
	</p>

	<Aside type="tip">
		Advanced demo (date split + remote JSON): the
		<a href="/examples/github-legends">GitHub Legends</a> 3D contribution skylines.
	</Aside>
</div>

<style>
	.quick-example__lead {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 0.75rem 1.5rem;
		margin-block-end: 1rem;
	}

	.quick-example__copy {
		min-width: 0;
	}

	.quick-example__copy :global(p) {
		margin-block: 0 0.75rem;
	}

	.quick-example__copy :global(p:last-child) {
		margin-block-end: 0;
	}

	/* Hug the CSV card on the right; don't stretch it full width */
	.quick-example__csv {
		min-width: 0;
	}

	.quick-example__csv :global(.copyable-csv) {
		margin-block: 0;
	}

	/* Tablet + desktop: copy left, CSV right */
	@media (min-width: 48rem) {
		.quick-example__lead {
			flex-direction: row;
			align-items: flex-start;
			justify-content: space-between;
			gap: 1.5rem 2rem;
		}

		.quick-example__copy {
			flex: 1 1 0;
			/* Keep readable measure */
			max-width: 36rem;
		}

		.quick-example__csv {
			flex: 0 0 auto;
			/* Sit on the right; shrink if viewport is tight */
			max-width: min(22rem, 46%);
		}

		.quick-example__csv :global(.copyable-csv) {
			width: 100%;
			max-width: 100%;
		}

		.quick-example__csv :global(.copyable-csv__scroll) {
			/* Table is short; allow full height in the side column */
			max-height: min(20rem, 55vh);
		}
	}

	/* Match Starlight expressive-code / pre look enough for shell one-liners */
	.quick-example__code {
		margin-block: 1rem;
		padding: 0.85rem 1rem;
		overflow-x: auto;
		border-radius: 0.5rem;
		background: var(--sl-color-gray-6, var(--sl-color-bg-nav));
		border: 1px solid var(--sl-color-gray-5);
		font-size: 0.875rem;
		line-height: 1.5;
	}

	.quick-example__code code {
		font-family: var(--__sl-font-mono, ui-monospace, monospace);
		background: transparent;
		padding: 0;
		border: none;
		font-size: inherit;
	}
</style>
